  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Find the minimum value of $\\frac{1}{7-3\\sin x}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac1{10}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}-1&\\le\\sin x\\le1\\\\-3&\\le-3\\sin x\\le3\\\\4&\\le7-3\\sin x\\le10\\end{align*}$$\nThe reciprocal is smallest when its positive denominator is greatest. Thus the minimum is $\\frac1{10}$, attained when $\\sin x=-1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
